 "disclosures": [
  "panel = local numpy build of the T-87 forward panel (data/cache/p1c_local, cutoff 2026-10-19); qfq close-to-close returns absorb cash-dividend adjustments (sidecars cash-only per r1067; raw close not reconstructable)",
  "suspension-resume transitions excluded (empty previous grid row)",
  "one-price bars excluded (limit boards are unexecutable and would concentrate into the calendar windows non-randomly)",
  "23 enumerated variants, zero multiplicity correction -- this is a descriptive scan, not a judged face and not a claim",
  "windows overlap in time (a day can be month-end + pre-holiday + Monday at once); variant counts therefore do not sum to the panel",
  "economic arithmetic is reported for turn-of-month and holiday families only; month/weekday rows are conditioning labels",
  "holiday breaks are derived from the trading calendar itself (gap >= 4 calendar days), not from an announcement table",
  "t values are inflated by cross-sectional correlation: the observation count is stock-days, not independent draws, so read the t as a ranking aid and the win-rate / year-stability columns as the honest strength signal (effective t is far smaller)",
  "the panel is the local rebuild, so this face is not byte-comparable with the r1074/r1076 CSV-panel censuses (same source family, different assembly)"
 ],
